{"slug":"/students/subjects/physics/mechanics/simple-machines/","source":"students/subjects/physics/mechanics/simple-machines.html","area":"students","kind":"content","title":"Simple Machines - Physics","description":"","subject":"physics","body":"<nav class=\"bg-white shadow-sm fixed top-0 w-full z-50\">\n        <div class=\"max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4\">\n            <div class=\"flex justify-between h-16 items-center\">\n                <div class=\"flex items-center\">\n                    <a href=\"/students/subjects/physics/mechanics/\" class=\"text-orange-600 hover:text-orange-800 mr-4\"><span class=\"mi -arrow-left\" data-mi=\"arrow_back\">arrow_back</span></a>\n                    <h1 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900\">Simple Machines</h1>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"text-sm text-gray-600 hidden sm:block\">Progress: <span id=\"progressPercent\">0%</span></div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </nav>\n\n    <main class=\"pt-20 pb-8 px-4 max-w-5xl mx-auto\">\n        <div class=\"bg-orange-50 border-l-4 border-orange-500 p-4 rounded-r-lg mb-6 animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-orange-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -bullseye mr-2\" data-mi=\"adjust\">adjust</span>Learning Objectives</h3>\n            <ul class=\"text-orange-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                <li>• Define simple machines and explain their purpose</li>\n                <li>• Describe six types of simple machines and their applications</li>\n                <li>• Calculate mechanical advantage, velocity ratio, and efficiency</li>\n                <li>• Explain how machines make work easier</li>\n            </ul>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 1: Introduction -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-orange-100 text-orange-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">1</span>\n                What are Simple Machines?\n            </h2>\n            \n            <div class=\"bg-orange-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-orange-500 mb-4\">\n                <p class=\"text-orange-800 font-medium\">A <strong>simple machine</strong> is a device that makes work easier by changing the magnitude or direction of a force.</p>\n            </div>\n\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">Simple machines do NOT reduce the amount of work - they make work easier by allowing us to use <strong>less force over a greater distance</strong> or change the direction of force.</p>\n\n            <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4\">\n                <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-blue-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -check-circle mr-2\" data-mi=\"check_circle\">check_circle</span>What Machines Do</h4>\n                    <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                        <li>• Multiply force (force multiplier)</li>\n                        <li>• Multiply speed/distance</li>\n                        <li>• Change direction of force</li>\n                        <li>• Transfer force from one place to another</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-yellow-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -cogs mr-2\" data-mi=\"settings\">settings</span>The Six Types</h4>\n                    <ol class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-1 list-decimal list-inside\">\n                        <li>Levers</li>\n                        <li>Pulleys</li>\n                        <li>Inclined planes</li>\n                        <li>Wedges</li>\n                        <li>Screws</li>\n                        <li>Wheel and axle</li>\n                    </ol>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 2: Key Terms -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-orange-100 text-orange-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">2</span>\n                Important Terms &amp; Formulas\n            </h2>\n\n            <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n                <div class=\"bg-green-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-green-500\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-green-700 mb-2\">Mechanical Advantage (MA)</h4>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded-lg text-center mb-2\">\n                        <p class=\"text-xl font-mono font-bold text-green-600\">MA = Load ÷ Effort</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\">The ratio of load to effort. MA &gt; 1 means the machine multiplies force.</p>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-blue-500\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-700 mb-2\">Velocity Ratio (VR)</h4>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded-lg text-center mb-2\">\n                        <p class=\"text-xl font-mono font-bold text-blue-600\">VR = Distance moved by effort ÷ Distance moved by load</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\">Also called \"Ideal Mechanical Advantage\" - the theoretical advantage based on geometry.</p>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"bg-purple-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-purple-500\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-700 mb-2\">Efficiency (η)</h4>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded-lg text-center mb-2\">\n                        <p class=\"text-xl font-mono font-bold text-purple-600\">Efficiency = (MA ÷ VR) × 100%</p>\n                    </div>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\">How well the machine works. Always less than 100% due to friction.</p>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 border-l-4 border-yellow-400 p-4 rounded-r-lg mt-4\">\n                <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-yellow-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -lightbulb mr-2\" data-mi=\"lightbulb\">lightbulb</span>Key Relationship</h4>\n                <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">Work input = Work output (ignoring friction)<br>\n                <strong>Effort × Distance<sub>effort</sub> = Load × Distance<sub>load</sub></strong></p>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 3: Types of Machines -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-orange-100 text-orange-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">3</span>\n                Types of Simple Machines\n            </h2>\n\n            <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n                <!-- Levers -->\n                <div class=\"bg-red-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-red-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-red-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -balance-scale mr-2\" data-mi=\"balance\">balance</span>1. Levers</h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm mb-2\">A rigid bar that rotates around a fixed point called the <strong>fulcrum</strong>.</p>\n                    <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-2 text-xs\">\n                        <div class=\"bg-white p-2 rounded\"><strong>Class 1:</strong> Fulcrum in middle (seesaw, scissors)</div>\n                        <div class=\"bg-white p-2 rounded\"><strong>Class 2:</strong> Load in middle (wheelbarrow, nutcracker)</div>\n                        <div class=\"bg-white p-2 rounded\"><strong>Class 3:</strong> Effort in middle (tweezers, fishing rod)</div>\n                    </div>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-xs mt-2\"><strong>VR</strong> = Distance from effort to fulcrum ÷ Distance from load to fulcrum</p>\n                </div>\n\n                <!-- Pulleys -->\n                <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-blue-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -circle-notch mr-2\" data-mi=\"pending\">pending</span>2. Pulleys</h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm mb-2\">A wheel with a groove that holds a rope or cable. Used to lift loads.</p>\n                    <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                        <li>• <strong>Single fixed pulley:</strong> VR = 1 (changes direction only)</li>\n                        <li>• <strong>Single movable pulley:</strong> VR = 2</li>\n                        <li>• <strong>Block and tackle:</strong> VR = number of pulleys</li>\n                    </ul>\n                </div>\n\n                <!-- Inclined Plane -->\n                <div class=\"bg-green-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-green-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-green-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -ramp-loading mr-2\" data-mi=\"help_outline\">help_outline</span>3. Inclined Plane</h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm mb-2\">A flat surface tilted at an angle to the horizontal. Makes lifting easier.</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\"><strong>VR</strong> = Length of slope ÷ Height of slope</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-500 text-xs mt-1\">Examples: Ramp, slide, mountain road</p>\n                </div>\n\n                <!-- Wheel and Axle -->\n                <div class=\"bg-purple-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-purple-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -circle mr-2\" data-mi=\"circle\">circle</span>4. Wheel and Axle</h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm mb-2\">A large wheel attached to a smaller axle that turn together.</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm\"><strong>VR</strong> = Radius of wheel ÷ Radius of axle</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-500 text-xs mt-1\">Examples: Steering wheel, doorknob, bicycle wheel</p>\n                </div>\n\n                <!-- Wedge and Screw -->\n                <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n                    <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-yellow-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -caret-up mr-2\" data-mi=\"arrow_drop_up\">arrow_drop_up</span>5. Wedge &amp; Screw</h4>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\"><strong>Wedge:</strong> Two inclined planes joined together (axe, knife, chisel)</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\"><strong>Screw:</strong> Inclined plane wrapped around a cylinder (jar lid, bolt, drill)</p>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 4: Interactive Simulation -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-orange-100 text-orange-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">4</span>\n                Interactive: Balancing Act\n            </h2>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">Explore how levers work with this interactive simulation:</p>\n            <div class=\"simulation-container bg-gray-100\">\n                <iframe src=\"https://phet.colorado.edu/sims/html/balancing-act/latest/balancing-act_en.html\"></iframe>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Section 5: Video -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"bg-orange-100 text-orange-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">5</span>\n                Video: Simple Machines Explained\n            </h2>\n            <div class=\"video-container bg-gray-100\">\n                <iframe src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/lBYYQValHWQ\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen=\"\"></iframe>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Practice -->\n        <div class=\"section-card animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n                <span class=\"mi -pencil-alt text-orange-600 mr-3\" data-mi=\"edit\">edit</span>Practice Questions\n            </h2>\n            <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n                <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">1. A machine has a load of 200 N lifted by an effort of 50 N. Calculate the MA.</p>\n                    <details class=\"mt-2\">\n                        <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer\">Show Answer</summary>\n                        <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                            MA = Load ÷ Effort = 200 N ÷ 50 N = <strong>4</strong>\n                        </div>\n                    </details>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">2. An inclined plane is 6 m long and 2 m high. Calculate its VR.</p>\n                    <details class=\"mt-2\">\n                        <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer\">Show Answer</summary>\n                        <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                            VR = Length of slope ÷ Height = 6 m ÷ 2 m = <strong>3</strong>\n                        </div>\n                    </details>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">3. A pulley system has MA = 4 and VR = 5. Calculate its efficiency.</p>\n                    <details class=\"mt-2\">\n                        <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer\">Show Answer</summary>\n                        <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                            Efficiency = (MA ÷ VR) × 100% = (4 ÷ 5) × 100% = <strong>80%</strong>\n                        </div>\n                    </details>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n                    <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">4. Give one reason why a machine's efficiency is always less than 100%.</p>\n                    <details class=\"mt-2\">\n                        <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer\">Show Answer</summary>\n                        <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                            Some energy is <strong>lost as heat</strong> due to:\n                            <ul class=\"list-disc list-inside mt-1\">\n                                <li>Friction between moving parts</li>\n                                <li>Work done against air resistance</li>\n                                <li>Energy used to lift parts of the machine itself</li>\n                            </ul>\n                        </div>\n                    </details>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Key Takeaways -->\n        <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-orange-50 to-amber-50 p-5 rounded-lg border border-orange-200 animate-fade-in-up\">\n            <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-orange-800 mb-3\"><span class=\"mi -star mr-2\" data-mi=\"star\">star</span>Key Takeaways</h3>\n            <ul class=\"text-orange-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n                <li>• Simple machines make work easier but don't reduce total work</li>\n                <li>• MA = Load ÷ Effort; VR = Distance<sub>effort</sub> ÷ Distance<sub>load</sub></li>\n                <li>• Efficiency = (MA ÷ VR) × 100% (always less than 100% due to friction)</li>\n                <li>• Six types: Lever, Pulley, Inclined plane, Wedge, Screw, Wheel &amp; axle</li>\n                <li>• Machines trade force for distance - use less force over greater distance</li>\n            </ul>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"flex justify-between items-center mt-8\">\n            <a href=\"/students/subjects/physics/mechanics/work-energy-power/\" class=\"px-4 py-2 text-gray-600 hover:text-gray-900\"><span class=\"mi -chevron-left mr-2\" data-mi=\"chevron_left\">chevron_left</span>Previous</a>\n            <a href=\"/students/subjects/physics/mechanics/momentum/\" class=\"px-4 py-2 bg-orange-500 text-white rounded-lg hover:bg-orange-600\">Next: Momentum<span class=\"mi -chevron-right ml-2\" data-mi=\"chevron_right\">chevron_right</span></a>\n        </div>\n    </main>","bodyClass":"bg-gray-50 min-h-screen","bodyStyle":"","css":["@keyframes fade-in-up { from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(20px); } to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); } }\n        .animate-fade-in-up { animation: fade-in-up 0.5s ease-out forwards; }\n        .section-card { background: white; border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.05); border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; }\n        .simulation-container { position: relative; width: 100%; height: 450px; overflow: hidden; border-radius: 8px; }\n        .simulation-container iframe { width: 100%; height: 100%; border: none; }\n        .video-container { position: relative; width: 100%; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden; border-radius: 8px; }\n        .video-container iframe { position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border: none; }"],"quiz":null,"tracker":null,"links":[]}